@lang en

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-application`
IMPORT `uk-interpretation-general`

-- Tests for uk-interpretation-general.l4. Each expected value was decided by reading the section and written down before the module was run.

§ `Section 1: words of enactment`

-- "Every section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment without introductory words." Sch 2 para 2: section 1 applies to Acts passed after the year 1850.
#ASSERT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 2000 1 1) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 1851 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 1850 12 31) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 1800 1 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 1 provides that a section of an Act takes effect as a substantive enactment, for an Act passed on` (YMD 1979 1 1) TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 14A(6): "specified"`

#ASSERT `section 14A(6) counts the period or day as specified` `in the subordinate legislation`
#ASSERT NOT `section 14A(6) counts the period or day as specified` `in the Act that confers the power or duty`
#ASSERT NOT `section 14A(6) counts the period or day as specified` `in some other instrument`

§ `Section 22(2): a reference to an Act`

-- A reference to an Act in a provision reaches an Act to which that provision applies.
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 1` (YMD 1960 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 1` (YMD 1850 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 6(b)` (YMD 1960 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 6(b)` (YMD 1979 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 14` (YMD 1950 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 14` (YMD 1880 1 1)
-- A provision that applies to an Act only in part still applies to it.
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 6(a)` (YMD 1800 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an Act in a provision` `section 9` (YMD 1800 1 1)
-- "this does not affect the generality of references to enactments or of the references in section 19(1) to other Acts"
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an enactment` `section 6(b)` (YMD 1960 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference to an enactment` `section 21` (YMD 1800 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference in section 19(1) to other Acts` `section 19(1)` (YMD 1800 1 1)
#ASSERT `section 22(2) reads the reference as reaching an Act passed on` `a reference in section 19(1) to other Acts` `section 19(1)` (YMD 2000 1 1)

§ `Section 23(2): enactments comprised in subordinate legislation`

-- Acts passed and subordinate legislation made after the commencement (on or after 1 January 1979, fork F9).
#ASSERT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1979 1 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2020 6 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1990 5 5), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2020 6 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2020 6 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) TRUE FALSE
-- Before the commencement the subsection gives nothing.
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1978 12 31), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1960 1 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23(2) counts the thing as an enactment` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1978 12 31), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) TRUE TRUE
-- "references to the passing or repeal of an enactment are to be construed accordingly" (fork F25)
#ASSERT `section 23(2) names the event for an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation as` `its passing` EQUALS `making`
#ASSERT `section 23(2) names the event for an enactment comprised in subordinate legislation as` `its repeal` EQUALS `revocation`

§ `Section 23(3), second limb: deeds and other instruments in section 17(2)(a)`

#ASSERT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1979 1 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2001 3 3), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2001 3 3), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 2001 3 3), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1978 12 31), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 23(3) counts the thing as an other enactment in section 17(2)(a)` (`An enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `subordinate legislation`, `the day it was passed or made` IS (YMD 1950 1 1), `what it says about coming into force` IS `no provision`) FALSE TRUE

§ `Section 25(2): references to the Interpretation Act 1889 and to other repealed enactments`

-- "as it applies to Acts passed at the time of the reference": the provision that the caller names as the corresponding one, taken as it applies to an Act passed on the day of the reference.
#ASSERT `section 25(2) — the extent to which the corresponding provision applies to a reference made on` `section 9` (YMD 1960 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 25(2) — the extent to which the corresponding provision applies to a reference made on` `section 6(b)` (YMD 1960 1 1) EQUALS `does not apply`
#ASSERT `section 25(2) — the extent to which the corresponding provision applies to a reference made on` `section 6(b)` (YMD 1979 1 1) EQUALS `applies without limit`
#ASSERT `section 25(2) — the extent to which the corresponding provision applies to a reference made on` `section 14` (YMD 1950 1 1) EQUALS `applies only so far as it relates to rules, regulations or byelaws`
-- Which provision corresponds to a repealed one is not in the text.
#ASSERT REFUSED `section 25(2) — the corresponding provision of the Interpretation Act 1978` "section 9 of the Interpretation Act 1889" BECAUSE "section 25(2) does not say which provision of the Interpretation Act 1978 corresponds to a provision of the Interpretation Act 1889 or of another enactment it repeals"
